-distinct-count of A distinct qualified inbound conversation after earned exposure: one conversation thread in inbound-response records and/or sales pipeline records where an eligible external contact from the card audience sends an inbound enquiry or reply after traceable earned exposure, and the thread meets agreed qualification criteria for coverage, expert discussion, partner or referral opportunity, enterprise-buyer interest or sales follow-up connected to The Stop Line proof. (events); excludes: Exclude outbound-only outreach with no inbound enquiry or reply, prepared or approved response records that do not contain an inbound conversation, spam, vendor solicitations, employee-only chatter, unqualified contacts or threads, duplicate records of the same thread, pre-exposure or untraceable conversations, and conversations not connected to earned exposure or The Stop Line proof.
+distinct-count of One distinct inbound conversation thread recorded in inbound-response records and/or sales pipeline records where an eligible external contact in the card audience, meaning a professional influencer, journalist, analyst, named expert or enterprise buyer reached through credible third parties, sends an inbound enquiry or reply after traceable earned exposure to The Stop Line. For this operational calculation, the thread qualifies when the record shows all of: observable audience eligibility; topic or intent tied to The Stop Line proof, proof-led earned coverage, expert discussion, partner or referral opportunity, or enterprise-buyer interest; attributable earned-exposure evidence before the inbound message; and enough recorded thread evidence to distinguish it from duplicates and irrelevant events. Count the conversation thread, not later lead qualification, booked meetings, sales follow-up, sales-qualified status, coverage publication or reporting completion. (events); excludes: Exclude outbound-only outreach with no inbound enquiry or reply sent by the external contact, prepared or approved responses that were not sent or published to the recipient, spam, vendor solicitations, employee-only chatter, duplicate records of the same thread, inbound messages before the traceable earned exposure, untraceable conversations, and conversations whose recorded topic or intent is not connected to The Stop Line proof or earned validation. Do not exclude otherwise eligible conversations merely because a later governance approval, sales follow-up, booked meeting, completed sale or coverage result did not occur.
